Task 3.1 – Choose the Layout Managers (3 Marks)
The library search screen needs a layout that keeps the search row and bottom buttons at a fixed preferred size while allowing the results area to expand when the window is resized.
Component / Container	Layout manager	Reason
Main JFrame	BorderLayout	Divides the window into top, bottom, centre and other regions.
Title panel	FlowLayout	Places the title at the top without stretching it unnecessarily.
Search panel	FlowLayout	Keeps the text field, category choice and Search button in one row.
Results panel	BorderLayout	Allows the results area to occupy the available centre space.
Bottom panel	FlowLayout	Keeps Prev, Next and Reserve buttons together at the bottom.
Status panel	FlowLayout	Displays the status message at the bottom.

Why BorderLayout?
- The centre region receives the extra space when the window grows.
- The top and bottom regions retain their preferred heights.
- The search and button panels keep their preferred component sizes.
- The results area automatically becomes larger or smaller.
